WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.260
Why do some neurons fail while their neighbours survive?

2
00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:10.740
No one yet knows. So how do you test one idea about it?

3
00:00:11.633 --> 00:00:12.673
Start with injury.

4
00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:17.833
When an axon is cut, the piece cut off from the cell body breaks into fragments

5
00:00:17.833 --> 00:00:18.833
within days.

6
00:00:19.583 --> 00:00:21.823
This was long thought of as passive wasting.

7
00:00:22.803 --> 00:00:27.183
It is not. The cut-off piece runs an active destruction program.

8
00:00:28.183 --> 00:00:33.403
In flies and mice, removing one gene, Sarm1, keeps the cut-off piece intact for

9
00:00:33.403 --> 00:00:34.403
weeks.

10
00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.947
Axons also degenerate in ALS.

11
00:00:37.767 --> 00:00:42.307
So the obvious next test is to remove Sarm1 from a mouse model of ALS.

12
00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:49.150
These mice make a mutant human SOD1 protein, and they develop motor neuron disease.

13
00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:54.190
Predict. Without Sarm1, will these mice live longer?

14
00:01:00.283 --> 00:01:03.303
No. Survival did not improve.

15
00:01:04.063 --> 00:01:07.183
Nor did the behavioural, nerve recording or tissue measures.

16
00:01:08.283 --> 00:01:11.283
Needed after a cut does not mean needed in this disease.

17
00:01:12.243 --> 00:01:14.423
The motor neurons may die by another route.

18
00:01:15.383 --> 00:01:17.763
And one mouse model is not human ALS.

19
00:01:18.763 --> 00:01:20.623
The result stays inside this model.

20
00:01:21.583 --> 00:01:25.123
Does this show axon loss does not matter in ALS?

21
00:01:25.123 --> 00:01:28.023
No. That claim goes too far.

22
00:01:28.967 --> 00:01:34.467
A better test measures axons, nerve-muscle contacts and cell bodies, as well as

23
00:01:34.467 --> 00:01:35.807
survival, in the same mice.

24
00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:39.310
The scorers should not know each mouse's genotype.

25
00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:42.510
Then the test is repeated in a second model.

26
00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:45.520
Here is what each result supports.

27
00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:48.400
Losing Sarm1 protects cut axons.

28
00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:52.440
In this model, losing it did not improve the disease measures.

29
00:01:58.533 --> 00:02:01.653
State what each result supports, and what it leaves open.

30
00:02:02.533 --> 00:02:05.613
Then design the next experiment to test what is still open.
